      "commit": {
        "parents": [
          {
            "commit": "fc01842f8542a35d18980696fdf3f316a234b444",
            "subject": "LU-18298 utils: do not write open a file to detach it from PCC"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Oleg Drokin",
          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-08-25 01:00:06.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Oleg Drokin",
          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-08-25 01:00:06.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-18298 tests: retry the PCC backend umount in sanity-pcc",
        "message": "LU-18298 tests: retry the PCC backend umount in sanity-pcc\n\numount_loopdev() waits for the backend mount to go idle by polling lsof,\nthen umounts once. That poll cannot see what usually holds the mount:\nan attached PCC inode pins it through pcci_path, and an open PCC copy\npins it through the file, and both are kernel references that belong to\nno process. lsof reports the mount idle on the first iteration, the\ngrace loop exits immediately, and the umount fails.\n\ncleanup_pcc_mapping() does not help here either, as lctl pcc clear frees\nthe dataset but detaches no inode, so any file still attached at cleanup\nkeeps the mount busy.\n\nRetry the umount itself instead, dropping the client caches between\nattempts. That releases the Lustre inodes and with them the PCC copies\nthey hold, which is what the loop was trying to wait for. Keep the lsof\ncall, it still reports a process holding the mount, which is the case\nthe old loop did handle.\n\nThis is what test_100 trips over: it attaches with projid={0}, so any\nroot owned file written under the mount during the run is attached, and\n\"umount: target is busy\" ends the test after everything it checks has\nalready passed.\n\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I09694d6eddc35d256649ac1af22fd5203ab57afe\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
